WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.238
Preview the four typing experiences with the learner’s readiness in mind.

2
00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:09.642
Paws and Keys Adventure is designed for ages four to nine and gentle progression.

3
00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:15.780
Story Sprint practices passages and reports speed, accuracy and character feedback.

4
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.771
Wordfall Reactor is a word-board challenge with everyday or optional subject vocabulary.

5
00:00:21.971 --> 00:00:26.306
Cipher Chase combines typing with steering and arcade demands.

6
00:00:26.506 --> 00:00:33.565
The course illustrations are concept art; the real screenshots and instructions show the actual controls.

7
00:00:33.765 --> 00:00:36.891
Begin with a short, personal accuracy goal.

8
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:42.629
Check whether the learner can read the text and use the controls without unnecessary strain.

9
00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:45.801
Do not make a public speed ranking the default.

10
00:00:46.001 --> 00:00:52.646
After a brief round, ask which keys or combinations caused difficulty and practice them slowly.

11
00:00:52.846 --> 00:00:58.784
Offer an untimed or off-screen alternative when the timed controls interfere with participation.

12
00:00:58.984 --> 00:01:03.057
If you use a curriculum passage, check the content separately.

13
00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:07.961
Typing the text accurately does not demonstrate that the learner understands it.

14
00:01:08.161 --> 00:01:15.611
Ask a new question without the passage visible, or require an explanation and example after a vocabulary round.

15
00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:22.987
Pause and choose one game, one readiness adjustment and one content question that would reveal learning beyond the

16
00:01:23.187 --> 00:01:24.278
game score.

